Apache-2.0
----------

- Dual Tachyon: the original UV-K5 firmware. The BK4819, ST7565 and UI
  helper drivers (core/Src/bk4819, core/Src/st7565, core/Src/ui) derive
  from it, as do parts of the V1 platform layer: the DP32G030 register
  headers (platform/uv-k5-v1-dp32g030/bsp/dp32g030/*.h) and the peripheral
  drivers (platform/uv-k5-v1-dp32g030/Src/peripherals/*).
- egzumer / reald: the ARDF fork of the UV-K5 firmware. The gain table and
  the squelch handling derive from it.
- armel: the UV-K1 / UV-K5 V3 (Puya PY32F071) port. Used as the reference
  for the V3 platform layer.
- Arm: CMSIS headers (platform/uv-k5-v1-dp32g030/external/CMSIS_5, and
  cmsis_compiler.h, cmsis_gcc.h, core_cm0plus.h in
  platform/uv-k5-v3-py32f071/bsp/py32f071/Include).


MIT
---

- muzkr: the UV-K5 V3 bootloader flasher (platform/uv-k5-v3-py32f071/tools/
  k5v3-flasher). It is vendored from muzkr's serialtool, which ships in
  armel/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom under tools/serialtool/, and it has been
  modified by this project (split-packet fix in msg.fetch, bounded ACK wait
  with resends, no page padding, verbose trace, BL-version prefix compare).
  See platform/uv-k5-v3-py32f071/tools/k5v3-flasher/README.md. The MIT
  copyright headers are preserved in each file; the licence text is in
  platform/uv-k5-v3-py32f071/tools/k5v3-flasher/LICENSE. ScoutFlasher uses
  this modified version for V3 radios.
- Marco Paland: printf (core/external/printf and
  platform/uv-k5-v1-dp32g030/external/printf).


BSD-3-Clause
------------

- Puya Semiconductor / STMicroelectronics: the PY32F0xx device headers and
  system files (platform/uv-k5-v3-py32f071/bsp). The CMSIS headers in the
  same folder are Arm's, see Apache-2.0 above.


Bundled binary programs
-----------------------

ScoutFlasher.exe contains two programs that are not part of this project's
source code. Both are included unmodified.

- K5TOOL v1.8.0.0 by qrp73, GPL-3.0. Used to flash UV-K5 V1 radios. It runs
  as a separate program. Source code: https://github.com/qrp73/K5TOOL
  (full licence text: tools/scout-flasher/bin/K5TOOL-LICENSE.txt).
- Prolific PL2303 USB-serial driver 3.3.11.152, Microsoft-signed,
  (c) Prolific Technology Inc. Included in ScoutFlasher.exe for
  compatibility with older programming cables. It is not part of the source
  tree.
